      <dt class="font-semibold">Required</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <ul>
      <li><code>name</code></li>
      <li><code>state</code></li>
      </ul>
      </dd>
      </dl>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Property</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Type</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Description</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>name</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>string</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>name is the required name of a specific gatherer. It may not exceed 256 characters. The format for a gatherer name is: {"{"}{"{"} gatherer {"}"}{"}"}/{"{"}{"{"} function {"}"}{"}"} where the function is optional. Gatherer consists of a lowercase letters only that may include underscores (<em>). Function consists of a lowercase letters only that may include underscores (</em>) and is separated from the gatherer by a forward slash (/). The particular gatherers can be found at https://github.com/openshift/insights-operator/blob/master/docs/gathered-data.md. Run the following command to get the names of last active gatherers: "oc get insightsoperators.operator.openshift.io cluster -o json \</TableCell>
